%%setfont-1 Symbol 13
%%setfont-2 Times-Roman 13

X: 1
T: What Is the World to Me?
C: Words: Georg M. Pfefferkorn, 1667.  Translated by August Crull, 1893, alt.
C: Music: 'Was Frag Ich Nach Der Welt' Ahasverus Fritsch, 1679. Setting: The Selah Song Book, 1926.
C: copyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2026 Revision.
S: Music source: "The Selah Song Book", 1926 Hymn 329.
S: Lyrics source: The Handbook to the Lutheran Hymnal, 1942  Hymn 430
S: http://www.projectwittenberg.org/etext/hymnals/tlh/world.txt 
S: Note that the text of this hymn from the Handbook to the Lutheran Hymnal is available on Project Wittenberg, 
S: operated by the Walther Library of Concordia Theological Seminary Fort Wayne and the text is listed as public domain.
S: 
S: Note that there is confusion about the translation date for this hymn as it is wrong in the usually-reliable 
S: TLH.  I find this in the "Evangelical Lutheran Hymn-book" by Lutheran Publication Board, Baltimore, 1893 Hymn 282
S: The mistake probably happened because it was translated well before the LCMS made an English language hymnal
S: so it was not published by CPH
S: 
S: Also note that the tune Darmstadt (Fritsch) or O Gott du Frommer Gott is an adaptation of this which affects 
S: both the tune and setting.  The adaptation was J. S. Bach.  But this is the original.  Some hymnals still 
S: label the modified tune as Was Frag Ich Nach Der Welt
M: 4/4 % time signature
L: 1/4 % default length
