%%begintext
%% 6. The world with wanton pride 
%% \tExalts its sinful pleasures 
%% \tAnd for them foolishly 
%% \tGives up the heavenly treasures. 
%% \tLet others love the world 
%% \tWith all its vanity; 
%% \tI love the Lord, my God, 
%% \tWhat is the world to me! 
%%endtext
%%multicol new
%%leftmargin 8cm
%%rightmargin 2cm
%%begintext
%% 7. The world abideth not; 
%% \tLo, like a flash 'twill vanish; 
%% \tWith all it gorgeous pomp 
%% \tPale death it cannot banish; 
%% \tIts riches pass away, 
%% \tAnd all its joys must flee; 
%% \tBut Jesus doth abide, 
%% \tWhat is the world to me! 
%%endtext
%%multicol new
%%leftmargin 13.5cm
%%rightmargin 2cm
%%begintext
%% 8. What is the world to me! 
%% \tMy Jesus is my Treasure, 
%% \tMy Life, my Health, my Wealth, 
%% \tMy Friend, my Love, my Pleasure, 
%% \tMy Joy, my Crown, my All, 
%% \tMy Bliss eternally. 
%% \tOnce more, then, I declare: 
%% \tWhat is the world to me! 
%%endtext
%%multicol end


